        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "My use case is/was a hand-rolled [grapple.nvim](https://github.com/cbochs/grapple.nvim) / [harpoon](https://github.com/theprimeagen/harpoon) replacement, originally posted here: https://www.reddit.com/r/neovim/comments/1sgu7yt/we_have_harpoon_at_home. That code worked well enough but the one thing I really missed was easily switching bookmarks when switching git branches. I kept thinking to myself \"if only I could namespace the marks, then I could list and go-to `<branch>:A`, instead of `A`\"\n\nI didn't know extmarks when I made the original post and honestly I still don't know them that well. A sticking point of the above is that you need to be able to store, visit, and manipulate these marks/bookmarks/etc somewhere potentially without any buffer loaded. Imagine a cold-open with no buffers. The buffer(s) haven't been read in advance first. Can extmarks do that? If so then probably this issue can be closed. If not, I think there may be room for improvement.",
